<article class="env-lemma" id="0E0Y">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0E0Y">Lemma <span data-tag="0E0Y">76.26.5</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $f : X \to Y$ be a flat morphism of locally Noetherian algebraic spaces over $S$. If $X$ is Cohen-Macaulay, then $f$ is Cohen-Macaulay and $\mathcal{O}_{Y, f(\overline{x})}$ is Cohen-Macaulay for all $x \in |X|$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      After translating into algebra using Lemma <a href="/tag/0E0W" data-tag="0E0W">76.26.3</a> (compare with the proof of Lemma <a href="/tag/0E0X" data-tag="0E0X">76.26.4</a>) this follows from Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/045J" data-tag="045J">10.163.3</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>